# App Review demo account for scripts/review_account.sh (skill heji-review-account). Sourced as bash.
# The password is never here: it lives in ~/Credentials/review-accounts.env and App Store Connect.

REVIEW_EMAIL="appreview+folio@hejitech.com"
# The Worker that serves POST /api/review-sign-in, and where it runs.
WORKER_DIR="projects/folio/services/web"
WRANGLER_ENV="production"
SITE="https://folio.hejitech.workers.dev"
BUNDLE_ID="com.hejitech.folio"

# App Store Connect › App Review Information › Notes.
REVIEW_NOTES="Folio is where people review what their AI agents (Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT and others, connected to Folio over MCP) make together: web pages and documents called artifacts.

Sign in: on the sign-in screen tap \"Sign in with email\" (below Continue with Google) and use the demo account above. People create accounts with Sign in with Apple or Google; email sign-in is only for accounts we hand out, such as this one. Each sign-in with it starts from demo data: two artifacts that different agents worked on (\"Big Sur weekend\" and \"Standing desks under \$600\"), an open suggestion from Gemini and comments.

What to try: open Big Sur weekend. Preview shows the page; Review has Gemini's suggestion (the changes and a preview), which you can accept or reject; Comments shows the discussion and lets you reply; History shows each version and what changed. The person icon at the top shares the artifact (invite links, view-only link). Settings > Notifications turns on alerts for agents' suggestions, comments and versions, with Accept, Reject and Reply on the notification. The share sheet in other apps (Safari, Photos, Notes) has \"Folio\" to save a page, text or photos as a new artifact.

Connecting an agent is optional and needs a computer or another AI app; the demo data shows what agents produce.

Account deletion: Settings > Delete my Folio data deletes everything Folio keeps about the account (artifacts, history, sharing, agent connections, devices) and signs out. The same sign-in also opens our other apps, so their data isn't touched."
